+
+The controller of \citet{dirusso_investigating_2023} walked on its original mechanical model in a local replay. SCONE is open-source software for simulating musculoskeletal motion and optimizing its control \citep{geijtenbeek_scone_2019}. I built the authors' version of SCONE, which included their spinal controller, and ran their saved parameters on their planar OpenSim model with nine degrees of freedom and 18 muscles. The model took 16 steps and advanced \qty{11.57}{\meter} in \qty{10}{\second}. A second run in a fresh process reproduced the trajectory. This recording supplies neural, force, and joint-motion references for testing a transfer.
